  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1153 AM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nUpper level winds will begin to back to the southwest early in the \nday in advance of a short wave trough moving northeastward across \nnorthern Mexico. Ascent does not appear to be very strong with this \nshort wave as it approaches the area late Thursday into Friday. Lift \nwill begin to spread overhead the area early Thursday afternoon \nlasting through Friday afternoon until the trough axis passes \noverhead. A strong low level jet will develop in response to this \nshort wave trough bringing significant amounts of isentropic ascent. \nStrong winds at 850mb will remain through the day time but shift \neastward through the day swinging over the Rolling Plains in the \nafternoon. Large scale subsidence will then move overhead beginning \nlate Friday afternoon ending precipitation. Precipitable water \nvalues will increase through the day on Thursday peaking early \nFriday morning with values ranging from one inch over the extreme \nsouthwestern Texas Panhandle to as much as 1.50 inches over the \nRolling Plains. Model soundings become completely saturated by \nsunset on Thursday afternoon. These values correspond to anomalies \nabove the 99th percentile for late October/early November. When \nprecipitation begins on Thursday afternoon, some instability will be \npresent with model soundings not quite saturated yet. However, as \nthe atmosphere becomes completely saturated by late Thursday \nafternoon, lapse rates will greatly weaken leading to little to no \navailable instability. Therefore, the best chances for any thunder \nwill be early on in the event Thursday afternoon. \n\nModels show another slower short wave trough hanging back late on \nFriday through early Saturday. However, model QPF amounts are light \nsuggesting this may only be low stratus or possibly drizzle. This \nsecondary short wave trough will move east of the area on Saturday \nafternoon leading to clearing skies for Halloween evening. Short \nwave ridging will move over top the area on Sunday in advance of \na deep long wave trough moving across the western CONUS. Models \nare struggling a fair bit with this next system early next week \nbut does look to bring a strong front through sometime from Monday\nthrough Tuesday next week.",
